 "response": "**ANSWER: $1905K**\n\n**Method**\n- Only Finance Office records change the budget. All other messages are rumours and were ignored. So were non-budget items such as audits and invoice batches.\n- The budget starts from #0001, which sets it to $1810K.\n- A withdrawn update counts as never having happened. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so its target stays in force.\n\n**Withdrawal chains that decided the outcome**\n- #0002 (\u2212$138K) is withdrawn. The chain is #1545 \u2192 #0504 \u2192 #0031 \u2192 #0018 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0002. #1545 voids #0504, which makes #0031 effective, which voids #0018, which makes #0005 effective.\n- #0066 (\u2212$456K) is withdrawn. #1184 voids #0545, which makes #0095 effective, which voids #0086, which makes #0083 effective.\n- #0035 (+$593K) stands. #0920 voids #0331, which makes #0176 effective, which voids #0119. That makes #0110 effective, which voids #0084, which makes #0078 effective, which voids #0069.\n- #0036, #0027, #0091, #0265, #0480 and similar chains were resolved the same way, working from the last withdrawal back to the target.\n- The two updates I nearly missed are also withdrawn: #0363 (by #1076) and #0675 (by #0922).\n\n**Result**\nApplying every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in order from $1810K gives a final budget of $1905K. This is a single running total, not checked by a second independent pass.\n\nANSWER: $1905K",
